{
    "word": "marmoreal",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "f4d14604-5282-3fd9-9efd-49dd13131833",
                "word": "marmoreal",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "abf99e7b-2cdc-472b-a5eb-2d60baaee11a",
                        "entry_id": "f4d14604-5282-3fd9-9efd-49dd13131833",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more marmoreal"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "940e3376-ae87-4566-8474-64d7df69e501",
                        "entry_id": "f4d14604-5282-3fd9-9efd-49dd13131833",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most marmoreal"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4941598b-46bc-3f08-beb9-b93a33cd8377",
                        "entry_id": "f4d14604-5282-3fd9-9efd-49dd13131833",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Resembling marble or a marble statue; cold, smooth, white, etc.; marblelike."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "literary"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ab8bcdef-b030-4cfb-9d95-b4abd01658e8",
                                "sense_id": "4941598b-46bc-3f08-beb9-b93a33cd8377",
                                "text": "How many a night serene, shall I behold / Those vvarm attractive orbits, close inshrined / In ether, over vvhich Love's column rose / Marmoreal, trophied round vvith golden hair."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2791cf1f-2b2f-4533-a0ee-184ca093d49e",
                                "sense_id": "4941598b-46bc-3f08-beb9-b93a33cd8377",
                                "text": "[T]he green / And glancing shadows of the sea did play / O'er its marmoreal depth: […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "92c0ca0e-96e0-4ba0-af0b-eafcdde203a2",
                                "sense_id": "4941598b-46bc-3f08-beb9-b93a33cd8377",
                                "text": "Each feminine delight of florid lip, / Eyes brimming o'er and brow bowed down with love, / Marmoreal neck and bosom uberous,— […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0d3fd223-6865-44d2-912a-022942734672",
                                "sense_id": "4941598b-46bc-3f08-beb9-b93a33cd8377",
                                "text": "The marmoreal whiteness of her perfect neck and firm, well-rounded arms was emphasized by a sharp contrast. Of color there was none, save for the slight flush of health in her cheeks and the rich, red line of her strong, sensitive mouth."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a32e518f-1d68-40e1-85c2-dcc9352399ac",
                                "sense_id": "4941598b-46bc-3f08-beb9-b93a33cd8377",
                                "text": "Youth's infinite choice of roads had given place to a rigid groove, presided over by a relentless marmoreal blonde."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1e946c4d-decf-4f5e-9b85-62aa48f6ba4d",
                                "sense_id": "4941598b-46bc-3f08-beb9-b93a33cd8377",
                                "text": "Irma had collapsed into a chair, and her long marmoreal face was buried in her hands."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c3740ff6-6783-43f3-a037-9498c31b5c30",
                                "sense_id": "4941598b-46bc-3f08-beb9-b93a33cd8377",
                                "text": "[I]f now the soldier's fingertips, the pads, seemingly endowed with a sudden clairvoyance, could sense through those different stuffs the hems of subterranean garments and even the very minute roughness of skin, pores and moles—if, as I said, his fingertips arrived at this, perhaps her flesh, marmoreal and lazy, was hardly aware that these were, in fact, fingertips, and not for example, nails or knuckles."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "277575ee-9745-4686-a6bf-69a9b5f0f40c",
                                "sense_id": "4941598b-46bc-3f08-beb9-b93a33cd8377",
                                "text": "The gods, of course, were a quite farcical invention, though necessary for the as it were marmoreal exaltation of the civic virtues."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cd824cf3-464f-3d0a-a95f-c53c599d2356",
                        "entry_id": "f4d14604-5282-3fd9-9efd-49dd13131833",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Made out of marble."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "literary",
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7bdb7e22-2ee4-4a0f-af8c-9e8d373805e5",
                                "sense_id": "cd824cf3-464f-3d0a-a95f-c53c599d2356",
                                "text": "But each night as he stood on that high marble terrace with the curious urns and carven rail and looked off over that hushed sunset of beauty and unearthly immanance he felt the bondage of dream's tyrannous gods; for in no wise could he leave that lofty spot, or descend the wide marmoreal flights flung endlessly down to where those streets of elder witchery lay outspread and beckoning."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4d79e325-3684-4167-a888-dc58f8230460",
                        "source_entry_id": "f4d14604-5282-3fd9-9efd-49dd13131833",
                        "source_sense_description": "resembling marble or a marble statue — see also marblelike",
                        "target_lang_word": "marmoréen",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "marmoréen",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "676cca15-e7c1-330c-948b-f5b19bcdedbf",
                                        "entry_id": "a77159da-e00c-3c6c-8fb8-2c2602240db7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui a la nature ou l’apparence du marbre."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b9a83bde-f593-4db1-968d-3f977a5bac35",
                                                "sense_id": "676cca15-e7c1-330c-948b-f5b19bcdedbf",
                                                "text": "La salle de danse offrit cette inoubliable invention, que le service fut fait par de belles filles aux formes impeccables qu’au moyen de draperies et de masques blancs on avait transformées en statues marmoréennes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7e27b3c5-f08b-41b0-b2e1-25c10733c5e5",
                                                "sense_id": "676cca15-e7c1-330c-948b-f5b19bcdedbf",
                                                "text": "Son pavage marmoréen arrivait jusqu’au bas des fenêtres actuelles."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c00c833a-73f0-4e92-bd98-1dd5c150834a",
                                                "sense_id": "676cca15-e7c1-330c-948b-f5b19bcdedbf",
                                                "text": "Partout le marbre blanc régnait. De la pierre marmoréenne émanait une douce clarté que les délicates nervures noires qui la parcouraient ne suffisaient pas à affaiblir."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "624d7543-fc10-4dcf-a961-9f7f0d96d13a",
                                                "sense_id": "676cca15-e7c1-330c-948b-f5b19bcdedbf",
                                                "text": "Calcaires marmoréens."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "28375752-22ad-3538-a172-9d391f041e91",
                                        "entry_id": "a77159da-e00c-3c6c-8fb8-2c2602240db7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui a l’apparence du marbre, des statues en marbre."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "881ce9ff-cd15-4b81-a6ce-361dfb927fc8",
                                                "sense_id": "28375752-22ad-3538-a172-9d391f041e91",
                                                "text": "Lors, sans tergiverser plus longtemps, notre excentrique demoiselle quitta ses voiles éthérés et plongea dans les flots son corps somptueux jusqu’à ses marmoréennes épaules."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3cbf360b-215b-451c-b4df-516bfb5a8c69",
                                                "sense_id": "28375752-22ad-3538-a172-9d391f041e91",
                                                "text": "Il faut lire, relire, re-relire, et presque apprendre par cœur le discours que prononça André Malraux, dans le vent glacé de cet hiver 1964, sous les yeux d’un De Gaulle plus marmoréen que de coutume."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5b529a99-f2aa-4b38-af20-70aa245ca6c2",
                                                "sense_id": "28375752-22ad-3538-a172-9d391f041e91",
                                                "text": "Le président a perdu la raison qui faisait de lui un être marmoréen et calculateur."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3fcc32d2-c3eb-451c-9094-1516efc42bd6",
                        "source_entry_id": "f4d14604-5282-3fd9-9efd-49dd13131833",
                        "source_sense_description": "resembling marble or a marble statue — see also marblelike",
